#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""amazing-grok — talk to Grok and dictate with it, from one hotkey.

Usage: amazing-grok tap|login|talk|dictate|stop|status|json

  tap      bind your hotkey to this. One press toggles dictation; a quick
           double press starts a voice conversation with Grok. While a
           conversation is running, any press ends it.
  login    sign in with your xAI account in the browser (OAuth + PKCE)
  talk     toggle a voice conversation (same as a double tap)
  dictate  toggle dictation (same as a single tap)
  stop     end whatever is running
  status   idle|recording|transcribing|talking|error
  json     waybar custom module payload

Dictation streams the mic to xAI's /v1/stt and types the words into the
focused window as you speak. A conversation streams the mic to the Grok Voice
realtime API (wss /v1/realtime) and plays Grok's answers; Grok can search the
web and X on its own (server-side web_search and x_search tools).

Auth is an xAI OAuth session, refreshed on demand. The refresh token is
single-use, so refresh happens under a lock file and the new grant is written
(atomically) before anything else can fail. A Wizard sign-in in
~/.wizard/xai_oauth.json is reused when there is no session of our own.
XAI_API_KEY works too.
"""
